On Sat, Oct 24, 2026 10:11 PM, Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org> wrote:
> Thanks for the v2 of 02/26. The series still can't go in as is, because
> 16/26 adds a NULL dereference in ax25_frames_acked(). ax25_clear_queues()
> purges ack_queue without taking ax25->lock, so the skb_peek() check above
> can be stale by the time skb_dequeue() runs, and skb_dequeue() can then
> return NULL. The old kfree_skb(NULL) tolerated that, but
> __skb_queue_tail(&acked, NULL) dereferences it in softirq context.

Hi Sasha,

You are right again, thanks.
ax25_clear_queues() purges the ack queue without ax25->lock, so the
skb_peek() test in ax25_frames_acked() can be stale and skb_dequeue()
can return NULL, which __skb_queue_tail() then dereferences.

I reproduced it in QEMU (6.12.94, two 4-CPU nodes with lockdep and
KASAN over a KISS link, four ROSE circuits sending 400 messages each),
simulating ax25_clear_queues() once between the check and the
dequeue: KASAN null-ptr-deref and a panic in ax25_frames_acked()
from the receive path. With the fix, no report under the same
simulation, and 1600/1600 messages in order on three normal runs.

v2 of 16/26 is attached for 6.12.y and 6.18.y. The loop now tests
what skb_dequeue() returns:

    while (ax25->va != nr && (skb = skb_dequeue(&ax25->ack_queue)) != NULL) {

Nothing else changes. Patches 17 to 26 apply unchanged on top of it,
and net/ax25 builds with W=1 and KASAN on both branches, with no
warning. The same fix is submitted to mod-orphan (pull request #42).

Out of curiosity, how did you spot these two? Is it part of an
automated review? I would like to run the same checks on the rest of
the AX.25, NET/ROM and ROSE code.

Thanks,
Bernard

